# AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md ship: an sdist is a source distribution, and
# someone building or contributing from it wants the guidance.
#
# Development notes deliberately do NOT ship — status, plans, roadmaps, anything
# written for whoever picks the work up next rather than for someone installing
# the package. They are not tracked at all (see .gitignore), because a tracked
# file in a public repo is a published file whatever this file says. What
# remains under docs/ is reference a reader of the package needs, and it is
# included wholesale below on that basis.
include AGENTS.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include CHANGELOG.md
recursive-include docs *.md
recursive-include examples *.py
# The suite ships, in full and on purpose. Someone building from an sdist --
# a distro packager, a security reviewer, anyone who does not trust a wheel --
# runs the tests, and this package's whole claim is that a connector's behavior
# is checkable. Declaring it explicitly also repairs a half-shipped state:
# setuptools' own sdist default quietly picks up `tests/test*.py` and nothing
# else, so `conftest.py` was being left behind. That file is the autouse
# fixture that hides installed third-party connector entry points, so without
# it the shipped suite's result depends on whatever else is in site-packages --
# green here, red on someone else's machine, for reasons in neither tree.
recursive-include tests *.py
# The bundled corpora are package DATA read at runtime from inside the installed
# package, so they must be in the WHEEL too -- that is declared in pyproject's
# [tool.setuptools.package-data]. They are listed here as well so the sdist
# carries them; without a corpus, `pip install "rag-connector[reference]"`
# installs a Reference RAG with nothing to point at.
recursive-include src/rag_connector/corpus *.txt *.md *.pdf *.docx *.rtf
# The frozen pre-chunked form of each bundled corpus, read at runtime by
# rag_connector.ingest.load_bundled_chunks. It is the substrate Pelorus's
# pre-canned extracts and RAGauge's pre-canned dataset both cite, so an
# install without it can serve the documents but not the ids anyone stored.
recursive-include src/rag_connector/corpus *.chunks.jsonl
